  "task4_3_null_result_SUPERSEDED_note": "SUPERSEDED: this original Task 4.3 result (n_real=20 target) had a search-window bug in _disordered_Bc_selfconsistent -- the coarse B-scan centered on the fixed clean ana=sqrt(mu^2+delta^2) instead of the per-realization rigid boundary, so at realistic W (10-46 Delta) the solver was searching far from where disorder had actually moved the boundary (per Task 4.1's own findings). This produced n_real=1-4 (out of 20 attempted) at every realistic W point -- NOT a valid ensemble average. Fixed by centering on the per-realization rigid boundary (bit-identical at W=0); see r9_disorder_methods.md and bdg_r9_disorder.py's _disordered_Bc_selfconsistent docstring for the full root-cause investigation. The corrected result is in task4_3_null_result above. Kept here, not deleted, per this project's standard of recording what changed and why.",
  "task4_3_rerun_wall_time_s": 4023.175416946411
}